WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
PlanRace is a proposed Bittensor market for verified query
optimization.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:11.775
Miners discover executable index plans. Validators check the results
on hidden workloads.

3
00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:18.675
This interim pitch presents verified localnet evidence. Public
testnet deployment remains pending.

4
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.075
A query can remain correct while becoming expensive as data and
workloads change.

5
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:30.700
Our proposed first users are database teams investigating recurring
performance regressions.

6
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:41.850
Centralized advisors offer strong integration. PlanRace explores
whether independent solvers can find useful alternatives under a
shared evaluation policy.

7
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.225
Buyer demand remains a hypothesis, not a customer result.

8
00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:51.350
The commodity is a bounded structured index plan for a known correct
query.

9
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.350
Miners can use search, learned systems, rules, or engine expertise.

10
00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:05.350
They receive public training information and a resource budget. They
cannot submit arbitrary executable code or their own timing claims.

11
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:09.600
Validators own the hidden fixtures and replay each artifact.

12
00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:16.000
A cryptographic commitment binds each task to its hidden fixtures,
engine, policy, and deadline.

13
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.800
Requests bind the intended receiver. Miner signatures bind submitted
artifacts.

14
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.775
After the deadline, the validator seals submissions and reveals the
secret seed and salt.

15
00:01:27.775 --> 00:01:32.475
Auditors can then regenerate the fixtures and verify the commitment.

16
00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:36.675
Exact results and policy compliance come before performance.

17
00:01:36.675 --> 00:01:44.700
Passing candidates face the same baseline across cold and warm
latency, setup cost, storage, and reuse horizons.

18
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:50.350
The protocol aggregates conservative measurements across workload
families and epochs.

19
00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:55.650
An all-fail round makes no new weight update. It does not clear old
on-chain weights.

20
00:01:55.675 --> 00:02:01.550
The committed simulation ran five hundred twelve seeded adversarial
replications.

21
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:08.450
It recorded zero false acceptance and zero exact-copy allocation
gain in those tested cases.

22
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:19.300
A material limitation remains: behavior-equivalent replicas improved
availability, with a worst allocation gain of thirteen point five
seven percentage points.

23
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:24.675
This is bounded simulation evidence, not a universal
Sybil-resistance proof.

24
00:02:24.675 --> 00:02:30.275
The verified local Subtensor run covered thirty epochs and six query
families.

25
00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:36.100
Three validator identities under one operator queried ten
heterogeneous miners.

26
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:45.000
The run recorded three hundred authenticated requests and two
hundred seventy signed responses, with finalized local-chain weight
readback.

27
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.325
These are localnet results. They do not demonstrate a public testnet
deployment.

28
00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:56.450
Bittensor can coordinate an open population of competing
optimization strategies.

29
00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.725
PlanRace separates open-ended discovery from bounded validator
replay.

30
00:03:01.725 --> 00:03:07.775
Cheaper verification is an economic hypothesis that must hold as
workloads scale.

31
00:03:07.775 --> 00:03:18.375
Disposable workers bound evaluation resources. Independent
operators, hardware calibration, and real buyer workloads still
require validation.

32
00:03:18.425 --> 00:03:24.850
The next proof gate is a dedicated public testnet run with
registered miners and validators.

33
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:31.825
It must produce signed interaction, scoring, finalized weights, and
a matching public metagraph readback.

34
00:03:31.825 --> 00:03:34.625
Test token funding remains outstanding.

35
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:47.350
Later work targets independent validators and production database
adapters. Current evidence uses generated SQLite workloads and does
not prove private-data safety or commercial demand.

36
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:52.475
PlanRace has a working local mechanism and public, auditable
evidence.

37
00:03:52.475 --> 00:03:58.150
HackQuest accepted the project submission with its testnet-pending
status disclosed.

38
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:03.925
The public repository and dashboard contain the implementation and
its limitations.

39
00:04:03.925 --> 00:04:13.475
This interim pitch does not replace the required testnet demo. The
final result section will change only when real chain evidence
exists.
